{"version": 2, "width": 124, "height": 34, "title": "UniMatch build \u2014 01-scaffold (rendered from the real Claude Code session log)"}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u276f user\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;37m  Read CLAUDE.md. Scaffold the UniMatch app:\r\n  \r\n  1. Initialize a Vite + React (JavaScript) project in the CURRENT directory (files at repo root, not a subfolder). Us\r\n  e `npm create vite@latest . -- --template react` conventions but you may write the config files directly \u2014 that's fa\r\n  ster than the interactive CLI.\r\n  2. Install dependencies.\r\n  3. Create the app shell: header with the UniMatch wordmark + tagline \"Find universities that fit your grades, your i\r\n  nterests, and your budget\", an empty main area with placeholder sections for Profile, Filters, and Results, and a fo\r\n  oter.\r\n  4. Create src/styles.css implementing the design language from CLAUDE.md (CSS variables for the palette, card styles\r\n  , buttons, inputs, chips, sliders, responsive grid).\r\n  5. Verify `npm run build` passes and fix anything that breaks.\r\n  \r\n  Do not build the matching logic or data yet.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[4.564, "o", "\u001b[1;32m\u23fa Bash\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m$ ls -la && node -v && npm -v\u001b[0m\r\n"]
